From a76b6b01d6ae186904edfa54c400751d0fd1fa5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Macready <william.macready@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:07:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(jax): fast vectorised scatter fold (opt-in,
 tolerance-compared)

scatter_mode='fast' on run_plan_positional/run_named folds the compute half into the destination with a single .at[].add over the static placement table (promise_in_bounds after a trace-time range check). Ordered stays the default and bit-exact. Exact only without collisions or with exactly representable partial sums; otherwise tolerance-compared. No Lean change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
